Package: zupdf
Title: Read, Assemble and Write 'PDF' Files
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Opens 'PDF' files and reads their metadata, pages, objects,
    streams, fonts, images and text in reading order; copies pages
    between files to split, merge, rotate and reorder them, and sets
    metadata, permissions and encryption; and writes new 'PDF' files from
    R with text, paths and images. Uses a bundled copy of the 'pdfio'
    library (<https://github.com/michaelrsweet/pdfio>), so no system
    library beyond 'zlib' is required. Untrusted input is bounded by
    limits on size, object count, stream size and nesting depth. Pages
    are never rendered to images.
